{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For Solomon</b> — <b>To the king give</b>: A prophecy of David, or one of the poets, concerning Solomon or concerning the Messiah, and it is a sign of lamed, like \"for the sake of,\" as in וללוי אמר (and to Levi he said) — כי תומיך ואוריך (your Thummim and your Urim), לנכח השם (before HaShem)." "<b>And Elohim began</b> — for the sake of Your judgments. The meaning is that HaShem gave him permission to execute the judgments of Elohim." "And likewise <b>and Your righteousness</b> — and that he be a judge of justice."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 72, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:58.444133948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}